<article class="env-lemma" id="03WU">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03WU">Lemma <span data-tag="03WU">29.58.8</span>.</a> Let $f : X \to Y$ be an étale morphism of schemes. Let $n \geq 0$. The following are equivalent </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
the integer $n$ bounds the degrees of the fibres, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
for every field $k$ and morphism $\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(k) \to Y$ the base change $X_ k = \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(k) \times _ Y X$ has at most $n$ points, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
for every $y \in Y$ and every separable algebraic closure $\kappa (y) \subset \kappa (y)^{sep}$ the scheme $X_{\kappa (y)^{sep}}$ has at most $n$ points. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This follows from Lemma <a href="/tag/03J5" data-tag="03J5">29.58.2</a> and the fact that the fibres $X_ y$ are disjoint unions of spectra of finite separable field extensions of $\kappa (y)$, see Lemma <a href="/tag/02GL" data-tag="02GL">29.37.7</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>